l ocation : Shanghai/Shenzhen/Guangzhou
Global Private Banking & Wealth
International Wealth and Premier Banking (IWPB) provides a leading premium proposition through Premier Banking and, together with our Private Bank, are present across the world’s most important markets, booking centres, and corridors most valued by our clients. Our wealth offering is further enhanced through our best-in-class manufacturing capabilities in Asset Management and Insurance. HSBC Private Banking helps high net worth and ultra-high net worth clients manage, grow, and preserve their wealth for generations to come. Our network of global experts helps clients access investment opportunities around the world, plan for future with wealth and succession planning, manage their portfolio with tailored solutions, and find the right support for their philanthropy.
We are currently seeking an experienced professional to join our team.
In This Role, You Will
To maximize HSBC's network in CIB, BB, IWPB, HK Business and UK Business to grow quality clients for PB;
To develop the collaboration strategies, and align interest with other line of businesses and other PB booking centers;
To manage collaboration activities between GPB China and other Global Businesses across markets including but not limited to Hong Kong, Singapore, United Kingdom, UAE and United States;
To establish attractive internal marketing programs and scheme to contribute prospecting and relationship building with internal partners and stakeholders;
To track and review collaboration effort, and provide insights to GPB management;
To ensure support from the partners from other Global Businesses and GPB market teams by proactively managing and strengthening the relationship with key stakeholders.
To be successful in the role, you should meet the following requirements:
Relevant qualifications and over 6 years of relevant experience in financial institutions;
Broad knowledge of universal banking model, with preference in corporate banking, investment banking and wealth management;
Strong data analytics and interpretation capabilities, and proficient in various MS office applications (ppt, excel etc.);
Fluent in English and Chinese speaking, and professional English writing;
Ability to think innovatively, shaping and communicating new concepts;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, in order to engage internal and external business stakeholders;
Experience in complex stakeholder management across organization is preferred – influencing, negotiating and partnering.
You’ll achieve more at HSBC.
HSBC is committed to building a culture where all employees are valued, respected and opinions count. We take pride in providing a workplace that fosters continuous professional development, flexible working and opportunities to grow within and inclusive and diverse environment. Personal data held by the Bank relating to employment applications will be used in accordance with our Privacy Statement, which is available on our website.
Issued by HSBC Bank (China) Company Limited

